WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.960
In this video, you will add an event to your calendar, and share it with a friend.

00:00:04.700 --> 00:00:05.420
We start on the map.

00:00:06.614 --> 00:00:08.374
Start at SoCal Lights dot app.

00:00:10.740 --> 00:00:13.160
On the home page, tap Use my location.

00:00:15.060 --> 00:00:16.040
Then tap Allow.

00:00:19.660 --> 00:00:22.080
Tap any event in the list to open it.

00:00:24.080 --> 00:00:28.840
Near the bottom of the event, beside Directions, is a row of small round buttons.

00:00:28.840 --> 00:00:30.940
The heart saves it to your favorites.

00:00:31.840 --> 00:00:32.840
The arrow shares it.

00:00:33.200 --> 00:00:34.920
And the calendar adds it to your calendar.

00:00:35.780 --> 00:00:36.600
Tap the calendar.

00:00:37.260 --> 00:00:41.780
On an iPhone, or when your maps app is Apple Maps, the site makes a calendar file.

00:00:42.360 --> 00:00:47.600
Open it, and the event goes into Apple Calendar or Outlook, with its date, time and place.

00:00:48.500 --> 00:00:54.340
If Google Maps is your maps app, it opens Google Calendar instead, with the event already filled in.

00:00:54.940 --> 00:00:55.820
Just tap Save.

00:00:56.500 --> 00:00:58.100
Now tap the share arrow.

00:00:58.100 --> 00:01:01.300
On a phone, it opens your phone's own share menu.

00:01:01.800 --> 00:01:03.920
Choose Messages, email, or any app.

00:01:04.520 --> 00:01:09.200
On a computer, the link appears, ready to paste into a message, an email, or a post.

00:01:10.000 --> 00:01:13.800
Whoever gets the link sees a preview card with the event's name and picture.

00:01:14.580 --> 00:01:17.000
When they tap it, the event opens on the map.

00:01:17.900 --> 00:01:20.860
That is how you add an event to your calendar, and share it.

00:01:21.440 --> 00:01:23.400
Do it for every event you do not want to miss.

00:01:24.900 --> 00:01:26.580
Next up: Save a night out.

